  <prompt>Replace PlaceholderTrapVerifier's T3 branch with a real Graph /servicePrincipals/{id}/appRoleAssignments query, comparing the live grant set against GraphAppRoles.cs's catalog (14 entries, 11 completed per task 005) -- correctly reporting the 3 still-null entries as a KNOWN GAP (not a false pass, and not a probe-breaking crash).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in H13's IE2ETrapVerifier/IE2EInvariantVerifier seam contracts and typed Azure SDK/REST post-condition verification.</role>

  <goal>T3's real verifier confirms the live Graph app-role assignment set matches GraphAppRoles.cs's completed 11-of-14 catalog, correctly distinguishing 'the 11 completed roles are all correctly granted' (Pass for those) from 'the 3 not-yet-completed roles are absent' (a documented, non-blocking known-gap classification, not a hard Fail that would permanently block acceptance on an unrelated pre-existing project risk item).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §6: 'T3 Graph app-role parity (14)... Graph /servicePrincipals/{id}/appRoleAssignments vs GraphAppRoles.cs (11 null GUIDs must be completed)... Blocked by: H10 + GUID completion (task 005 follow-through).' This project's risk register (plan.md §8) already tracks the 3-null-GUID completion as a SEPARATE, pre-existing risk item -- this probe's design must not silently conflate 'known incomplete catalog' with 'genuine grant failure'.</background>
    <relevant-files>
